 "_comment": [
  "ASK SKELETONS — one sub-ask each, in the four REGISTERS the real history",
  "actually uses (imperative / declarative / bare / polite). A row is one or",
  "more of these composed with a join from speech.json, then run through the",
  "speech layer. Placeholders follow the FastRule generator's contract",
  "(scripts/gen_fastrule_dataset.BASE_INFO): {event_title}->title,",
  "{task_title}->title, {item}->title, {date}->date_phrase, {time}->time_phrase,",
  "{name}->attendee, {query_range}->date_phrase. Slot suffixing (_2, _3, _4) is",
  "applied by the composer per ask position, so the skeletons stay unsuffixed.",
  "",
  "`content` names which content bank supplies the title, so the damage layer",
  "knows what it may attack: 'event'/'task'/'item' draw the plain banks;",
  "'possessive'/'compound'/'loanword' draw the damageable banks in speech.json.",
  "A skeleton with no title slot omits it."
 ],
